Chapter: MastermindWasm
  cites Games chapter Mastermind
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Mastermind, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. A code is one number under 1296 and would fit an
 i32 easily; what does not fit is the candidate POOL, which starts as all
 1296 codes and is filtered after every guess. So the page holds a handle to
 a state that carries the pool, defined here because the engine threads its
 pieces as separate arguments through `mm-guess-loop`.

 Nothing needs a copy in this chapter. `mm-filter-pool` builds its result by
 pushing onto an empty accumulator rather than writing through
 `list-set-at`, so filtering the pool does not disturb the pool it filters.
 The grader measures that rather than taking it on trust.

 A score is packed as blacks times ten plus whites, and 40 means solved.

 We say:

Section: The Handle

  MmState = record {
    secret     : Integer,
    pool       : List Integer,
    guesses    : Integer,
    last-guess : Integer,
    last-score : Integer,
    solved     : Boolean
  }

Section: The Browser Interface

  mm-wasm-new : Integer -> MmState
  mm-wasm-new (seed) =
    MmState { secret = mm-make-secret (rng-new seed), pool = mm-all-codes,
              guesses = 0, last-guess = (-1), last-score = (-1), solved = False }

  mm-wasm-step : MmState -> MmState
  mm-wasm-step (s) =
    if s.solved then s
    else if s.guesses >= 10 then s
    else if list-length (s.pool) <= 0 then s
    else let guess = list-at (s.pool) 0
    in let score = mm-score (s.secret) guess
    in let won = score == 40
    in MmState {
      secret = s.secret,
      pool = if won then s.pool else mm-filter-pool (s.pool) guess score (list-length (s.pool)),
      guesses = s.guesses + 1,
      last-guess = guess,
      last-score = score,
      solved = won
    }

  mm-wasm-secret : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-secret (s) = s.secret

  mm-wasm-pool : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-pool (s) = list-length (s.pool)

  mm-wasm-pool-at : MmState, Integer -> Integer
  mm-wasm-pool-at (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length (s.pool) then (-1)
    else list-at (s.pool) i

  mm-wasm-guesses : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-guesses (s) = s.guesses

  mm-wasm-last-guess : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-last-guess (s) = s.last-guess

  mm-wasm-blacks : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-blacks (s) = if s.last-score < 0 then (-1) else s.last-score / 10

  mm-wasm-whites : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-whites (s) = if s.last-score < 0 then (-1) else rng-mod (s.last-score) 10

  mm-wasm-solved : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-solved (s) = if s.solved then 1 else 0

  mm-wasm-done : MmState -> Integer
  mm-wasm-done (s) =
    if s.solved then 1
    else if s.guesses >= 10 then 1
    else if list-length (s.pool) <= 0 then 1
    else 0

  mm-wasm-score : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mm-wasm-score (secret) (guess) =
    if secret < 0 then (-1)
    else if secret >= 1296 then (-1)
    else if guess < 0 then (-1)
    else if guess >= 1296 then (-1)
    else mm-score secret guess

  mm-wasm-digit : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mm-wasm-digit (code) (pos) =
    if code < 0 then (-1)
    else if code >= 1296 then (-1)
    else if pos < 0 then (-1)
    else if pos >= 4 then (-1)
    else mm-digit code pos

